(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#" :text "Type definitions for AgentSlang Core IR. The Ssa* schemas are the contract the whole compiler lowers to: a module holds a string pool, ADT and record declarations, externs, globals and functions; a function is a list of basic blocks, entry first; a block binds block parameters, runs instructions in ANF (every operand is a value name) and ends in one terminator. Values are the boxed host Val (asl/host/src/value.h) unless typed raw i64, f64 or i1, which flow only through const, box, unbox, prim, opEntry, branch conditions, block parameters, direct-call parameters and returns, so the verifier proves them; prim is the raw arithmetic, compare, logic and conversion vocabulary listed by primSignature, where Int and Float never mix and integer overflow, division by zero and a float outside int64 trap; externs, builtins and closures take and return Val; a direct runtime entry (opEntry) is typed by builtinEntry. Joins use block parameters rather than phi nodes: an edge carries its arguments, so join arity is checked like call arity, a lowering emits a join as one parameterised block, and the LLVM emitter derives each phi from the incoming edges. The legacy Ir* statement schemas stay for asl-target-c, asl-target-llvm and asl-cli.")
