(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#SsaBuiltin.result" :text "Result type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#SsaBuiltin.kind" :text "wrap: no runtime entry, asl-target-llvm emits the call itself (ssa.asl helperEntrySym); intrinsic: call @llvm.<symbol>.f64 directly; libm: call @<symbol> directly, a libm declare")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#intrinsicEntry" :text "A math builtin lowered to the matching @llvm.<symbol>.f64 intrinsic instead of a runtime call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#libmEntry" :text "A math builtin lowered to a direct libm declare (@<symbol>) instead of a runtime call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#builtinEntries" :text "Builtins with a direct runtime entry, operand and result types as letters: v Val, i i64, f f64, b i1. Names starting with @, which source cannot spell, are entries the lowering fuses: @listHeadOr, @listTailOr, @listGetOr and @stringSliceOr compute (optionOr (listHead xs) d) and its kin without the Option; @listFirst and @listRest read a list a listEmpty? test found non-empty. floor, ceil, round and sqrt lower to their @llvm.*.f64 intrinsic (intrinsicEntry); pow, exp, log, log2, log10, sin, cos, tan and atan2 lower to a direct libm declare (libmEntry); both skip the runtime library entirely. The operator rows (+ - * / mod < <= > >= = != and not) type opEntry only: asl-target-llvm calls its @opsrt helpers for them (rtOps, ABIVAL-3) and abi.c defines no asl_rt_b_ entry for any row. The list and bytes rows (listTail, listHead, listEmpty?, cons, bytesLength, bytesAlloc, bytesGet, bytesSet) and the six fused rows type opEntry only: asl-target-llvm emits them as IR (ssa.asl nativeEntryName?, PRELUDEASL-B); so do the string rows (stringConcat, stringLength, stringFromInt64, stringSlice, stringStartsWith?, stringContains?, stringToBytes; ssa.asl stringEntryName? and formatEntryName?, PRELUDEASL-C), which sys.asl and its kin also emit as opEntry with raw operands; the frozen asl-target-c still names them in C it only syntax-checks.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#builtinEntry" :text "The direct runtime entry of a builtin called with arity operands, none when it has none and goes through asl_rt_builtin by name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/types.asl#primSignature" :text "Operand and result types of a raw primitive, none when the name is not one. The raw<Op><Width> family (plan IR-rawPrims) gives native code, never the checked Int/Float path, non-trapping i32/i64 arithmetic, bitwise and native pointer access: rawAddI64/rawSubI64/rawMulI64 and their I32 counterparts wrap on overflow with no trap (unlike addInt and kin, which trap); the i64 raw compares reuse eqInt/neInt/ltInt/leInt/gtInt/geInt, already raw i64 -> i1, so only the i32 compares (rawEqI32 etc) are new; rawAndI64/rawOrI64/rawXorI64 and their I32 counterparts are plain bitwise; rawShlI64/rawLshrI64/rawAshrI64 and their I32 counterparts take a shift count of the same width, masked to the width (63 or 31) by the emitter so every encoding, including a negative bit pattern, is defined, never poison; rawWidenI32 sign-extends i32 to i64; rawNarrowI32 truncates i64 to i32, failing through asl_rt_int_trap (NATIVE-trapMessage) when the value is outside -2^31..2^31-1: ERR_INT_OVERFLOW 'Int narrow leaves int32' (kind 7), a bare signal before this unit; rawPtrIsNull and rawPtrToInt read a ptr; rawIntToPtr (plan RT unit S6 round 3) is rawPtrToInt's mirror, one inttoptr, closing the gap sys.asl's own nanosleep/realpath :d's long noted (no way to build a null ptr constant, or any other raw-int-derived pointer, without a second real allocation standing in for NULL); rawLoadI8/rawLoadI32/rawLoadI64 read a native ptr buffer at an i64 byte offset (rawLoadI8 zero-extends to i32) and rawStoreI8/rawStoreI32/rawStoreI64 write it (rawStoreI8 truncates its i32 operand to i8), both trusting the caller's own bounds, as a native C store/load would; a store result is a dummy i1 true, the store's own effect being the point.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#" :text "Core IR verifier enforcing the closed vocabulary, ANF, and memory safety invariants; verifySsa checks the SSA contract: defined and dominating uses, existing blocks, known-call, closure, constructor, record and jump arities, switch exhaustiveness or default, unique definitions, string pool bounds, raw versus Val types and the operand and result types and arity of each raw primitive; a block unreachable from the entry counts as dominated by every block, as in LLVM")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#verifyStmt" :text "Diagnostics for one statement in its scope: a switch without default, a rebound name, a non-ANF operand or a unit stored in a nullable Option.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#VerifyState.env" :text "Current scope typing environment")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#VerifyState.diags" :text "Accumulated diagnostics")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#verifyFunction" :text "Diagnostics for a function: an empty body, a last statement other than return or jump, and every statement's diagnostics.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#verifyModule" :text "Diagnostics of every function in the module, in order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#verifyIr" :text "Ok when verifyModule finds nothing, else its diagnostics.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.arities" :text "Callable symbol to parameter count: module functions and externs")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.externs" :text "Extern declarations by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.functions" :text "Module functions by name, first definition wins")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.types" :text "ADT name to variants")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.records" :text "Record name to declared fields")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.globals" :text "Declared globals")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#SsaCtx.stringCount" :text "Size of the string pool")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefSite.block" :text "Defining block label, empty for function parameters and captures")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefSite.index" :text "Instruction position in the block, -1 for block parameters")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefSite.ty" :text "Value type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefState.defs" :text "Values defined so far, indexed by an AVL tree")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefState.diags" :text "Duplicate definitions found")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefWalk.state" :text "Definitions")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DefWalk.index" :text "Position of the next instruction")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DupState.seen" :text "Names seen")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#DupState.diags" :text "Duplicates found")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#InstrWalk.index" :text "Position of the next instruction")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#InstrWalk.diags" :text "Diagnostics so far")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#FnCtx.name" :text "Function name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#FnCtx.defs" :text "Value definitions, indexed by an AVL tree")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#FnCtx.blocks" :text "Blocks by label")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#FnCtx.entry" :text "Entry label")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#FnCtx.doms" :text "Block label to the labels dominating it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#FnCtx.retTy" :text "Return type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#variadicArgAllowed?" :text "C's default argument promotions pass only i32, i64, f64 (float promotes to double) or ptr through ...; i1 and val have no C representation there.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#classicRawName?" :text "True for the three raw types box and unbox move between Val and the register: i64, f64 and i1. ptr and i32 are raw too (ssaIsRaw?) but only a native (C ABI) extern carries them; they never box or unbox.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#verifySsaDiags" :text "Every violation of the SSA contract in the module, per function and block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#verifySsa" :text "Ok when verifySsaDiags finds nothing, else its diagnostics.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#dominatorSets" :text "Each block's dominator labels, itself included; an unreachable block maps to every label, the same as the iterative definition.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/verify.asl#domTree" :text "Cooper-Harvey-Kennedy idoms over reverse postorder, then dominator-tree pre/post numbers so a dominance query is O(1); replaces iterative O(B^2) set rounds (VERIFY-DOM)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/anfVerifyTest.asl#" :text "Acceptance gate for Task 53502: Typed Monomorphic ANF Core IR, Per-Profile Lowering, Verifier and Printer")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#" :text "Gate for raw ptr and i32 SsaTy and the variadic native (C ABI) extern (plan RT unit S2): a typed extern declared with ptr and i32 verifies and round-trips its types through ssaTyName/ssaIsRaw?; a variadic extern (ssaExternVariadic) accepts a call with more arguments than its declared arity and rejects one with fewer; an argument past arity is still type-checked against C's default argument promotions (i32, i64, f64 or ptr only, since i1 and val have no C representation there); a call that gets the declared argument types wrong is ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH with a clear message; box and unbox stay closed to ptr and i32 (ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH), since only i64, f64 and i1 move between Val and the register; an i32 constant outside -2^31..2^31-1 is rejected.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#getpidModule" :text "A typed native extern with no params returning i32: getpid() -> i32, called and its result discarded.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#writeModule" :text "A typed native extern write(i32, ptr, i64) -> i64: the ptr argument is a raw string-pool pointer (tyPtr), not a boxed Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#openModule" :text "A variadic native extern open(ptr, i32, ...) -> i32: a call may pass the mode argument past the declared arity of 2; it is still type-checked against C's default argument promotions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#openTooFewModule" :text "The same open extern called with only one argument: fewer than its declared arity of 2, which no variadic call may do.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#openVariadicBoolModule" :text "open called with an i1 as the vararg past arity 2: i1 has no C default-promotion representation in ..., so this is ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#openVariadicValModule" :text "open called with a boxed Val as the vararg past arity 2: val has no C default-promotion representation in ..., so this is ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#i32OutOfRangeModule" :text "An i32 constant one past INT32_MAX: ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#writeMismatchModule" :text "write's second parameter is ptr, but this module passes write a Val string constant instead: ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#boxPtrModule" :text "opBox of a raw ptr value: box and unbox stay closed to ptr and i32, so this is ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/externNativeTest.asl#unboxToI32Module" :text "opUnbox targeting i32: box and unbox stay closed to ptr and i32, so this is ERR_IR_TYPE_MISMATCH.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/irDocsTest.asl#" :text "Every exported function in asl-ir/src carries a doc, as the checker's rule-8 asks, read through asl-parser the way the compiler reads it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/irTest.asl#" :text "Comprehensive unit tests for asl-ir ANF representation, lowering, verification, and AST patching")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/linkTest.asl#" :text "Gate for multi-module link (plan SH unit M1): a 3-module fixture written to a fresh directory (app imports util and geom, util imports geom; an imported constructor, pattern, schema record and function value; size defined in all three modules) links to one verified SsaModule whose printSsa is the golden, with every symbol qualified by its module, the string pool and Option declared once; linking again prints the same text; a fixture prelude contributes only the functions the closure reaches and only the enums they use; an unexported name, an unknown alias and an unresolvable import are positioned diagnostics")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/linkTest.asl#evilPreludeSource" :text "LINK-userModuleNamedPrelude: a regular closure member that declares itself (module prelude ...) must be rejected, not silently preferred over the designated prelude for every colliding function name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/linkTest.asl#testPreludeNameClash" :text "LINK-userModuleNamedPrelude: preludeNeeds used to key off (.-name m), so a regular closure member named prelude was silently preferred over the designated prelude; loadClosure! now rejects it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerClosureTest.asl#" :text "Gate for AST to SSA lowering of closures and function values (plan SH unit I2c): a lambda lifts to a module function named after its declaration, its free variables passed as make-closure captures in first-use order; a call through a local name is call-closure; map, filter and fold, prelude functions since RT-PRELUDE P3b, take the closure Val as a call argument and their prelude closure is linked into the module; a module function used as a value is a capture-free make-closure; a nested lambda captures transitively; each lowers to a module that passes verifySsa and prints as its golden, and lowering is deterministic; a let-bound lambda calling itself is a positioned diagnostic")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerCorpusTest.asl#" :text "Ratchet gate for lowering the compiler's own closure (plan SH unit L2): linkEntry! on asl-compiler/src/compiler.asl (39 modules and the prelude; 24 since A6a imports asl-syntax core/tree into asl-parser, 25 since PARSER adds asl-parser/fnHeader, 29 since NETLOWER makes asl-target-llvm import asl-target-llvm/libc, sys, sysNet and sysRoute, 30 since SYSLOWER-b makes sysRoute import asl-target-llvm/sysProc, 31 since ABIVAL-1 makes asl-target-llvm/ssa import asl-target-llvm/rtFormat, 33 since PARASL makes asl-target-llvm/main import asl-target-llvm/parallel and asl-target-llvm/parRoute, 34 since ABIVAL-2 makes asl-target-llvm/ssa import asl-target-llvm/rtError, 36 since ARRLOWER-2 makes asl-target-llvm/main import asl-target-llvm/arrayRoute and asl-target-llvm/arrays, 37 since ABIVAL-3 makes asl-target-llvm/ssa import asl-target-llvm/rtOps, 38 since ABIVAL-4 makes asl-target-llvm/ssa import asl-target-llvm/rtObject, 39 since ABIVAL-5 makes asl-target-llvm/ssa import asl-target-llvm/rtValue), bypassing the checker, must yield a module that passes verifySsa; until it does, every remaining diagnostic must belong to a named blocker outside the lowerer, and each blocker's count may only shrink. startingTable is the count by code before L2, remainingTable the ratchet")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerDataTest.asl#" :text "Gate for AST to SSA lowering of data and short-circuit forms (plan SH unit I2b): and/or as branches into a join, enum constructors as construct, match as a tag switch with variant-field binds, some/none/ok/err as the prelude Option and Result, schema construction as record in declared order, field access and list literals each lower to a module that passes verifySsa and prints as its golden; malformed matches, constructors and records are lowering diagnostics at the declaration position")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerParityTest.asl#" :text "Gate for lowering the host dialect the compiler closure is written in (plan SH unit L2): the C-floor builtins as opBuiltin, a builtin or constructor used as a value as a lifted wrapper lambda, a nullary constructor atom as a construct, a computed call head as call-closure, a vector literal as a list, + and * over more than two operands as a left fold, unary minus, flat let bindings, else as a catch-all arm and :else as a rejected, non-wildcard pattern (ASL1-elseKeywordPatternParity), a bare constructor pattern, a non-exhaustive or armless match trapping through an unreachable block, host string escapes, and an indent-dialect enum whose field vector parses as (list ...); each lowers to a module that passes verifySsa and prints as its golden")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerTest.asl#" :text "Gate for AST to SSA lowering (plan SH unit I2): a recursive fib, a let/do/cond function and string, keyword, float, bool and unit literals, assert and refute lower to modules that pass verifySsa and print as the goldens below; constructs outside the subset come back as structured errors naming the construct and the declaration position")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerTest.asl#testHostVerbGone" :text "hostVerb left the lowered builtins in NX4: neither bare nor through a sys import alias does it lower.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerTest.asl#arityBuiltinSource" :text "Calls at the arity ARITY added a builtinArity row for: parMap and parFold without their slots operand (the default taken from the processor count, parallel.c's hostCpuCount), and the eight prelude.c file and environment builtins lower.asl had no row for at all. PRELUDEASL-P adds processSpawn/1 and processWait/2, called directly (processes) and processSpawn passed as a value (asValue), which the subset lowers as a lifted capture-free wrapper lambda. STANDINS adds the eleven sys.c builtins sysRouteTest and sysProcTest stood in for (sysInfo, sysMisc). SHIFTOPS adds << and >> at arity 2 (shifts).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerTest.asl#testPreludeNameClash" :text "PRELINK r2: a module function literally named prelude.stringJoin does not replace the prelude closure's stringJoin; the link reports the duplicate instead of keeping either body.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerAllocTest.asl#" :text "LOWER-ALLOC gate: per-unit lowering (lowerLinked, as tools/nativeTest.asl compiles a unit) of the asl-json/tests/jsonTest closure allocates below 134 MB, 0.6x the 224 MB measured interpreted on Darwin arm64 2026-10-10 at base f1a9ba193 (32 MB after LOWER-ALLOC); bytes are ASL_GC_STATS bytesAllocated of a units run minus a load-only run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerAllocTest.asl#main" :text "main MODE [ENTRY [DIR]]: load reads the closure of ENTRY (default the jsonTest suite) and the prelude; units also lowers every unit; lower adds the prelude functions they reach (lk/lowerPrelude); dump writes each lowered SsaModule's full structural text (str) to DIR/<name>.ssa, the golden corpus compared byte for byte across a lowering change.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerAllocTest.asl#runTests" :text "Runs load and units under ASL_GC_STATS on asl-host and asserts the lowering allocation (the difference) stays below 134 MB.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/patchTest.asl#" :text "Splice inversion gate: apply then invert is the identity on several trees, and a splice refuses to delete nodes it does not name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/printerTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for asl-ir IR and SSA printer")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/recordTyTest.asl#" :text "Schema identity is retained in Val-compatible SSA types for declarations, calls, joins and typed lets; a record type is a Val in the ABI, so it is never raw and a function value over it needs no wrapper; passing a record to a Val parameter keeps its identity; a typed let with a raw annotation converts the bound value where it binds, even when only a Val context uses it, and verifies; an annotated lambda parameter stays Val in the closure ABI while its record annotation, like a record capture, types it in the lambda body; a record returned or taken by a function of an imported module resolves through the import alias to that module's schema, at the call and in the extern, even when the importing module declares a schema of the same name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/ssaPrimTest.asl#" :text "Gate for raw primitive operations in the SSA IR (plan SH unit I1b): opPrim over i64, f64 and i1 verifies when operands and result carry the primitive's raw types; mixed i64/f64, Val operands, wrong result types, wrong arity and unknown names are rejected; the printer renders each primitive")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/ssaPrimTest.asl#testRawWellTyped" :text "The raw<Op><Width> family (plan IR-rawPrims): non-trapping i32/i64 arithmetic and bitwise, i32 compares (i64 compares reuse eqInt/ltInt etc, already covered above), widen/narrow, ptr null check and ptrToInt, and ptr load/store all verify at their declared raw types.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/ssaVerifyTest.asl#" :text "Gate for the SSA IR contract (plan SH unit I1): closures, ADT construct and switch, records, lists, string pool, globals and externs verify; undefined uses, missing blocks, arity mismatches, non-exhaustive switches without default and duplicate definitions are rejected; the printer is stable")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/tailrecParseLowerTest.asl#" :text "Regression gate: parser consumes the tailrec declaration modifier and LLVM IR lowering sees an ordinary function declaration.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#" :text "Multi-module link (plan SH unit M1): from an entry file, load the transitive import closure, resolving each import through asl-checker/resolve resolveImport!, the host loader's rules, from the importing file; lower every module once with lowerLinked, so every symbol is qualified by its declared module name; lower the prelude functions the closure calls, transitively, from asl/prelude/prelude.asl (the path the host loader falls back to); merge the modules into one SsaModule named after the entry module, threading one string pool through the lowerings, declaring each type and record once and keeping a prelude enum only when a function uses it; and verify the result. Modules come imports first, the entry last, then the prelude functions in the order they were first needed, then any native overlay functions, then any further prelude functions an opBuiltin resolved to. PRELUDEASL-0: after the closure and the prelude it reaches are lowered, a post-pass (rewriteModuleBuiltins) rewrites each opBuiltin whose name an ASL definition claims into an opCall of that definition, lowered and linked the same transitive, request-once way linkUnits already links ordinary prelude calls (seedExtend seeds the request from the opBuiltin names actually used, lowerExtra then pulls in whatever those definitions call inside the same unit). Lookup order: (1) asl/prelude/native/*.asl, a native-only overlay directory loaded as one synthetic LinkUnit named 'native' (the VM never loads it, so this is the only path that can shadow a C builtin with a native-compiled ASL definition); (2) asl/prelude/prelude.asl, already preferred over the C builtin by the VM, so an opBuiltin with a prelude definition (floatNan, floatInf, floatNegInf: the only three names both in lower.asl builtinArity and defined in prelude.asl at PRELUDEASL-0's base) now agrees between native and the VM; (3) otherwise the opBuiltin stays, asl_rt_builtin by name as before. A builtin used as a function value lowers through lower.asl's liftLambda into a wrapper function whose own body is an ordinary call of the builtin name, so the same instruction-level rewrite covers it with no separate case. Single-module lowerings with no link.asl closure (lowerSourceWith, lowerSourceLinked!, and asl-target-c emitC11Source beyond this file) are out of scope for this rewrite and keep calling the C builtin by name; asl-target-llvm emitLlvmSource (LOWERPQ) now goes through linkEntryBare!, so it gets this rewrite and the rest of a real closure (prelude plus file-based imports) while keeping its own entry module's declarations unqualified, as linkUnitsWithBareEntry's doc explains")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkUnit.path" :text "Source file")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkUnit.name" :text "Declared module name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkUnit.forms" :text "Parsed top-level forms")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkUnit.positions" :text "Declaration line:col by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkUnit.imports" :text "Import alias to the resolved file, in header order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LoadState.units" :text "Loaded modules, imports before their importers")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LoadState.seen" :text "Files already visited")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LoadState.diags" :text "Load diagnostics, in visiting order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LoadState.index" :text "Module index the resolver has built so far")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkAcc.strings" :text "String pool so far")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkAcc.modules" :text "Lowered modules, in link order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkAcc.requested" :text "Declarations already asked for, qualified unit.name, so the prelude and the native overlay share one list without their name sets colliding")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#LinkAcc.diags" :text "Lowering diagnostics")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#preludePath" :text "Path of the prelude the host loader falls back to, relative to the repository root.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#loadClosure!" :text "Load the entry file and its transitive imports, imports before their importers; err with every read, parse, resolve, duplicate-module and reserved-module-name diagnostic.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#importForms" :text "Map each import alias of a unit to the parsed top forms of its resolved dependency.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#allFunctions" :text "Collect all function definitions across a list of modules in order.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#preludeNeeds" :text "Prelude declarations the accumulated modules call and the prelude has not yet supplied; a module function that merely shares a prelude.<name> symbol does not count, so the clash reaches duplicateFunctions. Checked against .-requested while still qualified prelude.<name>, before stripping to the bare name lowerLinked's :only expects, so a name the native overlay also happens to define and has already requested (qualified native.<name>) never short-circuits this unit's own request.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#lowerPrelude" :text "Transitively lower unlowerable prelude references requested by accumulated modules until fixed point.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#nativeOverlayDir" :text "The native-only overlay directory (plan PRELUDEASL-0): each *.asl file in it is a module of top-level fns named after the C builtins they define; the VM never loads it, only linkUnits' opBuiltin rewrite does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#overlayTopForms!" :text "The defun, schema and enum top forms of one overlay file; ERR_LINK_READ or ERR_LOWER_PARSE when it cannot be read or parsed, since dropping a broken overlay file would silently fall back to the C builtin it shadows.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#overlayFormsAll!" :text "Every named overlay file's top forms in order, or the diagnostics of every file that failed to read or parse.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#nativeModuleHeader" :text "A synthetic (module native ...) header with no declarations of its own: lower.asl's moduleName reads a forms list's own header to name every function it lowers <module>.<name>, and the overlay's own files are stripped of their individual headers (overlayTopForms!) so their declarations land in this one combined 'native' namespace instead of each file's own.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#overlayUnitAt!" :text "dir's *.asl files as the 'native' LinkUnit; a missing dir is an overlay with no declarations, while a dir that exists but cannot be listed, or a file in it that cannot be read or parsed, is an error.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#overlayUnit!" :text "The native overlay directory as one synthetic LinkUnit named 'native': every overlay file's declarations concatenated under one module header, visible to each other unqualified as one module's own declarations are, and reaching the real prelude's functions unqualified through the usual LinkScope.prelude field when lowered by seedExtend/lowerExtra.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#builtinSeeds" :text "opBuiltin names the accumulated modules call that unit defines and that have not already been requested of it, qualified unit.name so a same-named prelude declaration requested separately (or vice versa) does not shadow this one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#lowerExtra" :text "Transitively lower unit's requested declarations until fixed point, as lowerPrelude does for the prelude itself, but with visible's own forms kept in LinkScope.prelude so unit's declarations can call visible's functions unqualified (lowerPrelude passes (list) here since the prelude extending itself already sees its own names through its own forms; the native overlay is not itself the prelude, so it needs the real prelude passed as visible).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#seedExtend" :text "The opBuiltin names unit resolves right now (the seeds), with acc extended by lowering them and then lowerExtra's fixed point for whatever they call inside unit. The seeds, not the full requested list lowerExtra may add past them, are what the opBuiltin rewrite below needs: only an opBuiltin instruction ever names one of them, since everything lowerExtra adds afterward is reached by an ordinary opCall.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#builtinRounds" :text "Overlay seeds, then the prelude its bodies call, then prelude seeds, repeated until a round seeds nothing new: a definition either step lowers may itself contain an opBuiltin the other unit (or an earlier step) claims, such as a prelude body calling an overlay name, which a single pass would leave on the C builtin. Terminates because every seed joins the requested list, which builtinSeeds excludes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#builtinTargets" :text "Each opBuiltin name the linked functions use, mapped to the linked definition that claims it, the overlay's before the prelude's; read from the functions actually lowered rather than from the seeds, so a name the prelude first reached by an ordinary call (isFinite? calling floatInf), and thus never seeded, is rewritten too.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#RewriteAcc.instrs" :text "Rewritten instructions so far, in order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#RewriteAcc.next" :text "Fresh temp counter for this function")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#coerceArgRewrite" :text "v, already Val (every opBuiltin operand is boxed), as the callee's param type: itself when the param is Val, else unboxed into a fresh raw temp.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#rewriteOne" :text "An opBuiltin instruction whose name resolved names a linked definition becomes a call of it, args unboxed to its param types and its result reboxed to Val when it returns raw, so the instruction's own dest keeps carrying Val for every existing consumer; any other instruction, and an opBuiltin resolved finds no definition for (or whose definition fnMap has lost, which cannot happen once lowered), passes through unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#rewriteBlock" :text "b rewritten, and the fresh temp counter after it: next starts where the function's previous block left it, since an SSA value is defined once per function, not per block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#rewriteModuleBuiltins" :text "An identity transform when resolved is empty (no program here calls a name the overlay or the opBuiltin-driven prelude lowering claimed), else the post-pass PRELUDEASL-0 adds: every opBuiltin naming a resolved key becomes a call of its linked definition.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#firstByName" :text "Deduplicate type declarations by name, keeping the first declaration encountered.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#firstRecordByName" :text "Deduplicate record declarations by name, keeping the first declaration encountered.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#duplicateFunctions" :text "One ERR_LINK_DUPLICATE_FUNCTION per symbol defined more than once across the lowered modules, such as a module function spelled prelude.<name> beside the prelude's own.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#emptyUnit" :text "A LinkUnit with no forms, imports or positions, named name; the fallback used when a real unit (e.g. the prelude) fails to resolve.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkUnits" :text "linkUnitsWith against the native overlay directory nativeOverlayDir.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkUnitsWith" :text "Lower every unit and the prelude functions they reach into one verified SsaModule named after the last unit, the entry; then PRELUDEASL-0's opBuiltin rewrite: the native overlay first, the real prelude's own opBuiltin-claimed names (floatNan and kin) second, each a seedExtend/lowerExtra fixed point like the prelude's ordinary opCall linking above, the pair repeated by builtinRounds until neither seeds a new name, and the name-to-callee map builtinTargets reads off the lowered functions rewritten into the merged module before it verifies. seedExtend's lowerExtra only chases the unit's own prefix (native.*), so a lowerPrelude pass follows it to resolve whatever real prelude.* names (bitAnd, bitOr, bitXor, ...) the overlay's own bodies called but no opBuiltin seed ever requests directly; without it, a program that reaches the overlay through no other prelude opBuiltin (floatNan and kin) links with those names only declared, never defined.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkUnitsWithBareEntry" :text "As linkUnitsWith, but the last unit (the entry) lowers through lowerLinkedAs with an empty prefix instead of its own module name, so its declarations stay unqualified and its diagnostic positions stay bare, matching lowerModule/lowerWithPrelude; every other unit, and the prelude, still lower module-qualified with path-qualified positions as linkUnitsWith always has. Shares finishLink's prelude/overlay/builtin-rewrite/verify tail with linkUnitsWith so the two differ only in how the entry unit's own lowering call is made.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkWith!" :text "Load the closure of the entry file and link it against the given prelude file.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkEntry!" :text "Load the closure of the entry file and link it against the host prelude at preludePath.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkWithBare!" :text "linkUnitsWithBareEntry against the given entry file and prelude file.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#linkEntryBare!" :text "Load the closure of the entry file and link it against the host prelude at preludePath, as linkEntry! does, but the entry module's own declarations stay unqualified and its diagnostic positions stay bare (no source path prefix); used by emitLlvmSource (LOWERPQ) so a caller passing a bare source string keeps the entry names and locus format it always has, while the prelude and any real file-based imports it names now resolve through the usual closure instead of being rejected.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#preludeUnitOf" :text "The prelude source as a LinkUnit located at preludePath; err when it does not parse or has no module header.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#lowerSourceWith" :text "Lower one standalone module as lowerSource does, its symbols unqualified, and link the prelude functions it reaches, transitively, from preludeSrc as prelude.<name>, the way linkUnits does for a closure; unverified, as lowerSource. A prelude that does not parse adds ERR_LINK_PRELUDE only when a name stays unresolved.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#lowerSourceLinked!" :text "lowerSourceWith against the host prelude at preludePath, read from the working directory.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#reservedPreludeNameDiags" :text "LINK-userModuleNamedPrelude: preludeNeeds keys 'defined' off (.-name m), so a regular closure member that declares itself (module prelude ...) lands in acc.modules under the same name as the designated prelude and is silently preferred over it for every colliding function name, with no duplicateFunctions diagnostic ever raised since the real prelude's version is never even lowered; reject the collision here instead of letting it corrupt linking\n'prelude' is reserved for the designated prelude every module links against; a regular import closure member declaring that name is a clear error, not a silent shadow. The designated prelude file itself is exempt, since loadClosure! on preludePath loads the prelude's own transitive closure under its own declared name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#" :text "AST to SSA lowering for the core subset (plan SH units I2, I2b and I2c): Int64, Float64, Bool, String, keyword and unit literals, strings unescaped as the host reader does; the arithmetic and comparison builtins and the host C-floor builtins, + and * over more than two operands as a left fold, unary minus; assert and refute, special forms in the host, as a builtin call with the condition and the optional message; if; cond, which gives unit when no clause holds and no else ends it, as the host does; and/or short-circuiting through branches; sequential let, its bindings as (name expr) pairs or flat name expr pairs; do; a vector literal as a list; direct calls of module functions, recursion included; module enum constructors and the prelude some, none, ok and err as construct, a nullary constructor atom included, with Option and Result declared only when used; an unqualified constructor of an imported enum when exactly one import declares it; match over one enum as a tag switch whose constructor arms, bare or applied, bind payload names by variant-field, whose arm _, else, :else or a name is the default, any arms after it unreachable and dropped as in the host, and which, like the host, traps through an unreachable block when neither exhaustive nor defaulted or when it has no arms; schema construction by :field pairs, evaluated in source order and stored in declared order; .-field access; list literals; (fn [params] body) lambdas lifted to module functions named <declaration>@lambda<n>, a spelling the lexer rejects in source, with free variables in first-use order as make-closure captures, nested lambdas capturing transitively; a module function used as a value as a capture-free make-closure, a builtin or constructor used as a value as a lifted wrapper lambda; a call through a local name or a computed head as call-closure; listSortBy, optionMap, resultMap and resultMapErr, and the prelude map, filter and fold, taking the closure Val; a let-bound lambda calling itself is a diagnostic. An enum case's field count skips the nameless field the indent dialect's (list ...) rendering of the field vector adds. Values are typed: Int64, Float64 and Bool annotations give a function a raw signature, every main staying Val as the program entry; literals are raw; arithmetic and comparison over raw operands of one type are raw primitives that fail as the host does (a Val operand of an Int or Float operation is unboxed, since Int and Float never mix), a builtin with a runtime entry is an opEntry typed by builtinEntry, any other a builtin over boxed operands; values are boxed at lists, constructors, records, closure calls and captures and Val parameters, unboxed with a run-time check where a raw type is needed, and a box or unbox made for a value is undone by reusing its source; a join takes the raw type its arms share when every arm has it, and is Val when any arm is Val; (optionOr (listHead xs) d), its kin over listTail, listGet and stringSlice, and a match on (listHead xs) or (listTail xs) never build the Option; a module function with a raw signature used as a value is a lifted Val wrapper, and a lambda unboxes its captures and annotated parameters on entry. Strings are unescaped and interned once in the module string pool. An if or cond closes the open block with a branch and joins its arms in one block whose parameter carries the result. Anything outside the subset is an IrDiag naming the construct and the function with its declaration line:col, and every failing declaration reports; the parser keeps positions per declaration only, so a construct inside a body is located by its function. lowerLinked lowers one module of a linked closure (plan SH unit M1): its functions, lifted lambdas, enums and schemas are named <module>.<name>; alias/name calls, function values, constructors, patterns and schema constructions resolve through the LinkScope imports to exported declarations, an unknown alias or an unexported name being a diagnostic; prelude enums are visible unqualified below the module's own names, prelude functions below the builtins of the subset")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Ctor.typeName" :text "Enum declaring the variant, qualified by its module when linking")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Ctor.variant" :text "Variant name as declared")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Ctor.arity" :text "Payload field count")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.arities" :text "Callable functions by source name, own and alias/name imported, to parameter count")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.late" :text "Prelude functions by name when linking, consulted after the builtins of the subset")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.ctors" :text "Variant constructors by source name, module enums over the prelude Option and Result")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.records" :text "Schemas by source name, fields in declared order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.defaults" :text "Schema defaults: schema name to map of field to default expression")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.types" :text "Module enums in source order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.targets" :text "Function and schema source names to their symbols; a name absent here is its own symbol")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.foreign" :text "Imported and prelude enums, for match exhaustiveness")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.aliases" :text "Import alias to module name, when linking")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.hidden" :text "alias/name of a declaration its module does not export, to that module")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.linked" :text "Lowered as part of a linked closure")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModInfo.sigs" :text "Signature of each callable by source name, own and imported over the prelude")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#FnSig.params" :text "Parameter types")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#FnSig.ret" :text "Return type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LinkScope.path" :text "Source file, prefixed to declaration positions")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LinkScope.imports" :text "Forms of each imported module by import alias")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LinkScope.prelude" :text "Prelude forms, visible unqualified below the module's own names and the builtins of the subset; empty for the prelude itself")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LinkScope.strings" :text "String pool the module extends")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LinkScope.only" :text "Declarations to lower, every one when none")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerCtx.fnName" :text "Declaration being lowered")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerCtx.pos" :text "Its line:col, or ? when the source is not known")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerCtx.info" :text "Module declarations")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Arm.kind" :text "ctor, wild or var")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Arm.variant" :text "Variant of a ctor arm, as declared")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Arm.typeName" :text "Enum of a ctor arm")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Arm.binds" :text "Payload names of a ctor arm, _ for an unbound field")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Arm.name" :text "Name a var arm binds to the scrutinee")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Arm.body" :text "Arm body forms")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#KeyedExpr.key" :text "Field name without its colon")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#KeyedExpr.expr" :text "Value expression")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.next" :text "Next value number")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.labels" :text "Next if or cond number")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.strings" :text "Module string pool")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.done" :text "Finished blocks, latest first")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.label" :text "Label of the open block")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.params" :text "Parameters of the open block")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.instrs" :text "Instructions of the open block, latest first")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.lifted" :text "Lambdas of the declaration lifted to module functions, innermost first")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.lambdas" :text "Next lambda number in the declaration")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.types" :text "Type name of each raw or record-typed value, indexed by an AVL tree; other values are Val")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LowerState.twins" :text "Each value a box or unbox made to the value it came from, which dominates it and is reused instead of converting back")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Lowered.st" :text "State after lowering")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Lowered.value" :text "Value holding the result")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LoweredList.st" :text "State after lowering")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LoweredList.values" :text "Values holding the results, in order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Bound.st" :text "State after the bindings")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Bound.env" :text "Source names to value names")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LoweredFn.function" :text "The lowered function")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LoweredFn.lifted" :text "Its lambdas as module functions")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#LoweredFn.strings" :text "String pool after it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Lambda.params" :text "Parameter names")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Lambda.types" :text "Type each parameter's annotation names, Val when it names no raw type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Lambda.body" :text "Body forms")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModAcc.strings" :text "String pool")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModAcc.functions" :text "Lowered functions, in source order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#ModAcc.diags" :text "Diagnostics, in source order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#builtinArity" :text "Operand count of a builtin the lowering emits as opBuiltin, -1 when variadic, none when the name is not one. Only builtins the host defines in C or lowers inline by name (& | ^ ~ << >>, NATIVE-INTRINSICS): a plain prelude function lowers from prelude.asl source, never a by-name runtime lookup. Every row is a contract on the native backend: it runs the builtin as emitted code of its own or rejects the call at build time, asl-target-llvm with ERR_LOWER_UNSUPPORTED naming the builtin (ssa.asl builtinDiags), never a link error, since asl_rt_builtin and prelude.c's core table left libaslrt.a (PRELUDEASL-Z). parMap and parFold's row is their full arity (slots given); builtinAltArity gives the shorter one, slots omitted. A cond dispatch on name rather than mapGet over a rebuilt mapFromPairs: ASL has no module-level constant to build the table once (ARITY-HOIST), so the table was reconstructed on every call; string = short-circuits per clause instead. & | ^ ~ also have a plain ASL body in prelude.asl (LANG-BITOPS-SYM) that asl-host runs directly; this row only governs native lowering, where bitPrim/typedBuiltin emit them as a single instruction over raw operands or an Int-checked @mathrt helper over boxed ones (NATIVE-PERF) instead of compiling that ASL body.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#builtinAltArity" :text "A second valid operand count for a builtin whose shorter call omits the argument asl-host's C builtin (parallel.c bParMap/bParFold) and the native routed wrapper (asl-target-llvm/parallel) both default the same way: the host's CPU count as parMap's and parFold's slots. A cond dispatch rather than mapGet over mapFromPairs, same reason as builtinArity (ARITY-HOIST).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#builtinArityFor" :text "The arity to lower a call of name with argc operands against: its primary arity, any count when that is variadic, else its alt arity when argc matches that instead, else none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#coerce" :text "The value v as type want: itself when it has that type, else boxed, unboxed (checked at run time) or both.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#coerceAll" :text "Each value coerced to the type at its position in wants, Val past its end.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#condition" :text "A branch condition: an i1 or a Val as it is, any other raw value boxed so the branch rejects it at run time as the host does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#unicodeEscape" :text "Code point and chars taken after u, -1 when malformed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#unescapeChars" :text "Exactly the host reader escape set; others fail.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#annotTy" :text "The raw type a primitive annotation names, or schema-known Val for other annotations.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#sigOf" :text "The signature a function lowers to: raw where its annotations name Int64, Float64 or Bool, Val elsewhere and for every main, the program entry.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#functionValue" :text "A module function as a closure value; one with a raw signature through a lifted wrapper taking and returning Val, the closure ABI.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#joinTy" :text "The one raw type among the values when every value has it, else Val: a Val arm is never unboxed to a raw arm's type, since nothing proves its kind (an N or T body the checker never saw, the prelude or an imported module, may yield an Int on one path and a Float on another), so the raw arms are boxed and a raw consumer unboxes once, checked, after the join.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#convertExit" :text "The finished block of the exit passes its value as type t: the value it was converted from when that has type t, else converted before the jump to the join.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#joinExits" :text "Close the open block with a jump carrying last to joinL and open joinL, whose parameter has the type joinTy picks for last and every earlier exit, a finished block label and the value it passes, each converted in its block.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#elseTest?" :text "CHECKER-condKeywordTruthy: :else is no longer a cond catch-all, only the bare else symbol; a keyword cond test, including :else, is rejected earlier by check.asl's Bool type check, so lowering never sees one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#bindTyped" :text "The value a typed let binds: v converted to a raw annotation's type; v, boxed when raw, tagged with a record annotation's schema; v itself for any other annotation, whose type it already has.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#binaryKind" :text "The raw type a binary builtin computes in: both operands' when they share one; for arithmetic and ordering, where Int and Float never mix, the raw operand's when the other is Val; else empty.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#binaryPrim" :text "The primitive computing the builtin in raw type k as asl-host does, empty when none does.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#bitPrim" :text "The raw primitive of a bit operator over two raw Int64 operands (NATIVE-INTRINSICS): & | ^ as one and/or/xor, << and >> as shl and ashr with the count masked to 0..63 as prelude.c does (rawShlI64, rawAshrI64), empty when either operand is a Val, whose Int check and want text stay in the @mathrt helper.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#notOn" :text "~ over a raw Int64 as xor with -1, one instruction (NATIVE-INTRINSICS).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#typedBuiltin" :text "A builtin over lowered operands: a raw primitive when the operand types select one, else its direct runtime entry with operands coerced to the entry's types, else asl_rt_builtin by name over boxed operands.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerField" :text "(.-f base): an opField over the base as a Val; when the base is a tyRec whose schema declares f Int64, Float64 or Bool (withFieldSigs), the read is unboxed to that raw type at once (checked at run time, so a record holding another type there fails as the unbox does), which the LLVM emitter fuses into one typed field read and arithmetic over it stays raw (NATIVE-PERF).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#armFamily" :text "The type the arm's pattern names: its (constructor ...) head's when bare is false, its bare constructor name's when true; empty otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#matchFamily" :text "The type an mt tests: its first (constructor ...) pattern's, else its first bare constructor name's; empty when no arm names one, as the host's matchFamily (compile.c) and the checker decide.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#listMatch" :text "The entry reading the payload when a match on (listHead xs) or (listTail xs), its arms Option constructors or _, can test the list instead of building the Option; empty otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerListMatch" :text "A match on (listHead xs) or (listTail xs) as a listEmpty? branch: the some arm binds the payload the entry reads, the none arm runs on the empty list, _ stands in for a missing one, and a variant with no arm traps as the switch would.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#unboxNamed" :text "Each name whose type at its position is raw rebound to its value unboxed on entry, and each whose type is a record typed by its schema, a closure's captures and annotated parameters arriving as Val.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#preludeName?" :text "name reaches the prelude function: no local or module function shadows it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#builtinName?" :text "name reaches the builtin: no local, module function, constructor or schema shadows it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#optionSource" :text "The fused entry computing (optionOr e d) when e is a call of listHead, listTail, stringSlice or the prelude listGet, empty otherwise.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerOptionOr" :text "(optionOr (f a ...) d) as the fused entry over a ... d, evaluated in source order, never building the Option.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#kindReturned" :text "The receiver kind a call's result has, from its concrete or generic name (and the receiver's kind where the result follows it); empty when not one of the closed set.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#genericStar" :text "The concrete builtin a receiver-independent generic name (head, split, keys ...) aliases, or empty; string dispatch instead of a table map rebuilt per atom (LOWER-ALLOC).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#genericKinded" :text "The concrete builtin a receiver-dependent generic name (length, get, slice ...) resolves to for receiver kind, or empty; the names are exactly those genericMulti? accepts.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#addLowered" :text "acc with a lowered function and its lifted lambdas pushed in reverse onto acc.functions; lowerWith reverses the list once, so the module keeps source order without a quadratic append per function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#resolveBinding" :text "One (name expr) or (name Type expr) binding with its value resolved, and the kinds its name adds: the annotation's kind, else the value's.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#schemaDefaults" :text "A schema's field defaults: the :default expression an ast/AstField already carries, parsed once by the reader when the field was read; a field with no :default clause is absent from the map, an omitted Option field included, since a default is declared, never inferred from a type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#fieldSigKey" :text "The sigs key holding a schema field's raw type: schema is the schema's symbol (a tyRec's name); the spelling, with a colon, names no callable.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#withFieldSigs" :text "sigs plus, for every field of s declared Int64, Float64 or Bool, its raw type under fieldSigKey (NATIVE-PERF), so a field read on a tyRec base yields that raw type (lowerField).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#defaultThunkBareName" :text "A schema field default's thunk fn name, unqualified: <Schema>$default$<field>, a spelling the lexer rejects in source")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.arities" :text "Callable source names to parameter count")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.ctors" :text "Constructor source names")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.records" :text "Schema source names to fields")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.defaults" :text "Schema source names to field defaults")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.targets" :text "Source names to symbols")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.foreign" :text "Enums declared by other modules")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.hidden" :text "Unexported alias/name to its module")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.sigs" :text "Callable source names to signatures")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#belowModule" :text "The prelude's declarations as a module sees them: its functions leave the callable names, to be reached after the builtins of the subset.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#targetSources" :text "Each target symbol of info.targets mapped to the first qualified alias/name (in key order) that targets it, built once per module so externSig does not rescan every target per extern (LOWER-ALLOC).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#externSig" :text "The signature of extern symbol n with its schema names resolved as a call through the alias/name that targets n (looked up in sources, see targetSources) resolves them.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerModule" :text "Lower the parsed forms of one standalone module, positions naming each declaration's line:col in diagnostics.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerWithPrelude" :text "Lower one standalone module, its own symbols unqualified as lowerModule names them, with the prelude visible as in lowerLinked: a call of a prelude function that no module function or builtin of the subset shadows is a call of prelude.<name>, left for the caller to link.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerLinked" :text "Lower one module of a linked closure, qualifying its symbols by module name and resolving imports and the prelude through the scope.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerLinkedAs" :text "lowerLinked, taking the qualifying prefix explicitly instead of always reading it off moduleName forms. An empty prefix (locatedPositions, linkedInfoAs) keeps this module's own declarations unqualified and its diagnostic positions bare, as lowerModule/lowerWithPrelude leave them, while every import and the prelude still resolve and qualify exactly as lowerLinked's own moduleName-prefixed call does; lowerLinked is now lowerLinkedAs called with moduleName forms, unchanged.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#declPositions" :text "Map each declared name to the line:col of its first declaration line in the source. Walks srcLines with fold (one pass, carrying the running line index in the accumulator) rather than folding over (range 0 n) and calling listGet srcLines i per line, which walked i cons cells per line for an O(n^2) cost on an n-line source (DECL-POSITIONS); output is byte-identical to the old implementation (declPositions inserts names in the same line order, so the resulting Map's key order and values match).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#lowerSource" :text "Parse the source and lower it as a standalone module; a parse error is one ERR_LOWER_PARSE diagnostic.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#floatText?" :text "the host reader's float: [+-]digits, then .digits and/or [eE][+-]digits")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#schemaDefaultAcc" :text "naming a private fn of this module resolves here, never in some importer's call site scope\na schema field default is lowered once here, in its own declaring module's ctx, as a zero-arg\nthunk fn; a constructor call anywhere just calls that thunk (visWithSchemaDefaults), so a default")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#caseArity" :text "the indent dialect renders a [...] field vector as (list ...), whose head parses as a nameless field")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#visWithSchemaDefaults" :text "never by re-lowering the raw expression at each constructor call site's own scope\na field default is resolved by calling its thunk, compiled once in the schema's own module (lowerTop),")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/arityAllocTest.asl#" :text "ARITY-HOIST gate: builtinArity (asl-ir/lower) used to answer every call by rebuilding (mapFromPairs (list ...163 pairs...)) and mapGet over it; it now dispatches with cond over string =, so a call costs a chain of string comparisons instead of 163 pair/cons/map allocations. testArityCorrectness checks the dispatch still agrees with the old table at its edges (first, last and an unknown name, and builtinArityFor's alt-arity fallback for parMap/parFold). testArityAllocation runs this file a second time as 'asl-host run ... arity', which loops builtinArity 20000 times over the table's last entry (its worst case for a cond chain) and nothing else, and asserts the (:gcStats ...) line's objectsAllocated for that run stays far below what the old table-rebuilding implementation cost for the same loop (measured ~317.68M objects on base; the cond dispatch measures ~23K), so reverting the fix fails this assertion.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/declPositionsAllocTest.asl#" :text "DECL-POSITIONS gate: declPositions folded over (range 0 (listLength srcLines)) and called listGet srcLines i per line, each listGet walking i cons cells into the line list, so an n-line source cost O(n^2); it now folds over srcLines directly, carrying the running line index in the accumulator, one cons step per line. This gate repeats lower.asl's own source (its largest module, ~1930 lines) 10x to ~19300 lines and times one declPositions call with procRusage: the quadratic version measured ~7.5s CPU on this fixture, the linear version ~0.7s, so the bound (2.2s, ~3x the linear time) fails on the old implementation and passes on the new one. A separate check run over every tracked .asl file (asl-host run against both implementations) confirmed declPositions's output is byte-identical except for lower.asl itself, whose own source text differs between the two versions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#functionBuiltinRefs" :text "names of the builtins the instructions of f call, block by block, repeats kept")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#definedNames" :text "names of the unit's top-level fn definitions, in source order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/link.asl#rewriteModuleBuiltinsAgainst" :text "m with every builtin call that resolved maps to a function rewritten to call that function, looked up among m's own functions and callees; m itself when resolved is empty")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#" :text "LOWER-QUAD-REST and VERIFY-DOM gate: lowering a synthetic program with n=800 enum, schema and import declarations allocates at most 2.15 times n=400, verifying n=1000 diamonds at most 2.3 times n=500 (each measured in a bounded child through tools/fleet/run), and dominatorSets equals the old iterative algorithm on every function of the checkSemanticTest closure and on loop, unreachable and chain shapes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#Vis.foreign" :text "newest first; infoOf restores declaration order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/declPositionsAllocTest.asl#repeatOnto" :text "DECL-POSITIONS: declPositions folded over (range 0 (listLength srcLines)) and called listGet srcLines i per line, each listGet walking i cons cells into the line list, so an n-line source cost O(n^2). This gate repeats lower.asl's own source 10x (its largest module, ~1930 lines, so ~19300 lines here) and bounds the CPU time a single declPositions call may take; the quadratic version measured ~7.5s CPU on this fixture, the linear fold-over-srcLines version ~0.7s, so the bound sits at roughly 3x the linear time.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lower.asl#keyedLiteral" :text "the keyed literal a positional one means: each declared field paired with the value in its position")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/declPositionsAllocTest.asl#lineOfLineStart" :text "lineOfLineStart finds the 1-based line of a '\nNEEDLE' anchor: the match index sits on the newline ending the line before NEEDLE's own line, so the line number is 2 past the newline count strictly before that index (1 to land on the anchor's own line, 1 more because the matched newline itself is not counted in the slice before idx).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/declPositionsAllocTest.asl#assertExactPosition" :text "DECLPOS-GATE-EXACT: a mutant that shifts declPositions' line numbering (e.g. (+ i 1) -> (+ i 2) in the fold) still passed this gate before, since it only bounded CPU time and the found-name count; these 3 assertions check exact 'line:col' for names whose expected position is derived independently from a fresh, single read of lower.asl (not the fixture, and not via declPositions itself), so a uniform or partial line-number mutation is caught.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#chainFunction" :text "a chain of n diamonds: every join branches on a value defined in the entry block, so each use asks whether the entry dominates a block n levels down")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#testLowerIsLinear" :text "allocation is deterministic, so the bound is tight: n=400 vs 800 measured 2.93x before LOWER-QUAD-REST, 2.06x after (map-backed n log n), 2.20-2.45x with any one of its fixes reverted (W4LOWER, 2026-10-10)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-ir/tests/lowerScaleTest.asl#testVerifyIsLinear" :text "n=500 vs 1000 diamonds (3n+1 blocks), deterministic bytes of verifySsaDiags: 4.24x with iterative dominator rounds, 2.15x with Cooper-Harvey-Kennedy and pre/post dominance queries (VERIFY-DOM, 2026-10-10)")
